{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Lane f041, criterion #7 evidence:\n- Gerrit change 3038 patch set 3 (b927d7c45f61) received Verified +1 from CI run 39183705544 (all jobs green, including pytest ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 and macos py3.13) and LLM-Review +1. It was submitted revision-scoped and MERGED at 2026-10-19 01:46:11 UTC (2026-10-18 18:46 PDT) as 21dabcbb2c1fab1da7f81ccfd5a1aaedc2f2bdaf on origin/main.\n- Node steps: run 39183705544 still ran \"Pin the Node toolchain\" and the npm cache on its Ubuntu cells. The Verified lane takes the workflow definition from trusted main (pre-merge at that point) and only the tree from the change. The first Verified runs on the post-merge definition show 0 Node/npm steps in all 3 Ubuntu pytest cells: 39186980558 (change 3040 PS1, head 21dabcbb2c1, 30 steps per cell) and 39187896857 (change 3040 PS2, 29 steps per cell).\n- `make verify`: NOT met locally. The single run on patch set 1 exited 2 with 18 failed and 20,191 passed. 1 was this change's regression (the `PromptWriteError` taxonomy entry), fixed in patch set 1 before push. 17 are wiki-render/pandoc tests that fail on this arm64 host because the bundled pandoc is x86_64 and no `PYPANDOC_PANDOC` 3.9 is configured (documented in docs/local-dev-env.md; host defect frenzied-snively-llama). `make verify` was not re-run. Its `make test` selection is the same as CI's gating ubuntu py3.13 cell, which passed on patch set 3."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792375658004431438,"uuid":"df59503d-e457-4227-a85e-4d7b91cfc293"}